  "id": "COMPOUND:31794 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "Linustatin is implicated in the biological pathway leading to RWLeu4 through multiple independent routes, all of which involve the Malme-3M protein as a common intermediate. The evidence suggests that Linustatin acts as a target for several compounds, including 2-(1a,4-dimethyl-3,3a,4,5,6,7,7a,7b-octahydro-2H-naphtho[1,2-b]oxiren-7-yl)prop-2-enoic acid, Notoamide B, and Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, which in turn target RWLeu4. This indicates that Linustatin may exert its biological effects through a shared mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of Malme-3M, which is a key player in the pathway leading to RWLeu4. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Linustatin to influence cellular processes through a central node, Malme-3M, thereby linking it to RWLeu4 in a complex but interconnected network.",
